Get reflection and speed right away (Sokoban may have the amulet if
you haven't done it yet, thereby saving a wish). Your strength is
already quite sufficient and isn't as important as the first two
extrinsics, so I'd defer wishing for gauntlets. After that, you'll
either have +0 or +3 boots and an elven helm and cloak to enchant. If
you have leather gloves, it's worth enchanting them too, since you'll
have plenty of resources to enchant magic gauntlets later on. Then,
since you've identified scrolls of identify, enchant weapon, charging,
and enchant armor, a magic marker is a *no brainer* wish.

I'd get my AC to -20 or so pronto. I'd also enchant Grayswandir
pronto, since it effectively doubles its enchantment when dealing
damage, and #twoweapon will be *that much easier* with a highly
enchanted main weapon. Also, enhance saber to skilled, since
#twoweapon uses the minimum of your weapon skill and twoweaponing
skill when determining your chance to hit.

Since you've effectively identified the "nice" scrolls, I might also
suggest a wand of polymorph if you have 10 or more junk scrolls (I
consider unidentified 100 zm scrolls "junk"). Scrolls of enchant
weapon and enchant armor are extremely common, and polypiling blessed
scrolls for a few scrolls of enchant weapon saves tons of marker
charges and holy water. If you already have a wand of polymorph, *do
this* when polypiling the spare armor from Ludios.

After that, if you want to buff your character, I'd wish for two
cursed scrolls of genocide, head to Sokoban, barricade the corridor
leading to the upper-left portion of the bottom level with a boulder,
strip clothes and weapon, and nurse dance at least once. You will most
likely gain at least 70 HP, and if you polypile later you'll be
grateful you identified the scroll. The other scroll could be used for
tengu (teleport control!) or more nurse-dancing. You could also charge
up a ring of increase damage, as Grayswandir will double its damage
too. Charging a ring to +5 is quite safe, effectively giving a +15
bonus through #twoweapon. Since polypiling for rings is easy with
enough scrolls of identify, it may not be worth a wish, but hey, the
more you know...

You have an incredibly strong character. Your enemies are now bag of
holding explosions, mind flayers, green slimes, cockatrice mishaps,
and all the other nasties that can YASD an endgame-ready character. Be
careful, and best of luck!


